Experiment 7: Outage Probability, LCR & ADF in SISO for SC and MRC

Aim

To study outage probability, Level Crossing Rate (LCR), and Average Fade Duration (ADF) in SISO system using Selection Combining (SC) and Maximal Ratio Combining (MRC). 


---

Short Theory

Small Scale Fading

Small scale fading causes rapid fluctuation in received signal strength due to:

Reflection

Scattering

Diffraction





---

Doppler Shift Formula

f_m = \frac{v f_c}{c}

Where:

 = mobile velocity

 = carrier frequency

 = speed of light



---

Coherence Time

T_c = \frac{9}{16\pi f_m}

If:

 → Slow fading

 → Fast fading





---

Level Crossing Rate (LCR)

LCR is the rate at which signal crosses a specified threshold level.

For Rayleigh fading:

L_R = \sqrt{2\pi} f_m \rho e^{-\rho^2}




---

Average Fade Duration (ADF)

ADF is the average time for which signal remains below threshold.

\bar{t} = \frac{e^{\rho^2}-1}{\rho f_m \sqrt{2\pi}}




---

Outage Probability

Probability that received signal falls below threshold level.

P(R)=1-e^{-\frac{R^2}{2\sigma^2}}




